design_plan.md content — Stage 1 plan:

# T5-R1-Flash Design Plan — Flagship Vehicle Battery
Case: t5_r1_flash
Task: ED ≥ 500.94 Wh/kg; 4C fast charge without Li plating; T_max ≤ 60 °C (333.15 K)
Date: 2026-08-25

## 1. Objective decomposition
| Metric | Threshold | Layer | Lever directions | Trade-off note |
- energy_density_wh_kg ≥ 500.94 (stage2): system (high-V cathode / high-cap anode), architecture (thin collectors/separator, thick electrodes), mass reduction. Trade-off: thicker electrodes → more heat, worse plating margin.
- plated = false at 4C (stage3): thin negative, small particles, high σ/t⁺ electrolyte, moderate current density; temperature helps but capped.
- T_max ≤ 333.15 K at 45 °C ambient → ΔT ≤ 15 K over 4C charge: cooling h + low DCR.

Priority: ED is the binding constraint (500.94 is far beyond conventional); safety constraints (plating/T_max) are hard gates.

## 2. Candidate strategy
R1 baseline: Chen2020 1C discharge SPMe + calc-energy + 4C_charge_45C (thermal lumped, plating). Ceiling assessment: best-possible Chen2020 architecture (10 µm Al / 6 µm Cu collectors, 9 µm separator, ε=0.25 electrodes, high-σ electrolyte) → expect ~380–450 Wh/kg → gap to 500.94 confirmed → escalate to Stage 2.
R2 materials: 
  - Electrolyte formulation (σ/t⁺ override, e.g., high-conductivity LiFSI-based) + molecular additives funnel (FEC/VC/LiFSI/LiBOB) for SEI/plating suppression.
  - System switch: LNMO high-voltage cathode (4.7 V, `--base LNMO.json`) vs OKane2022 (NMC811/graphite+SiOx, cracking model).
  - Electrode composition (run-comp): high-energy doped NMC (e.g., Li-rich or Si/Mg-doped) — only if budget allows (CUDA env).
R3+: combine best system + architecture (thin everything) + electrolyte + cooling h; iterate; 1C discharge (SPMe→DFN) + calc-energy + 4C safety per round.
Closing: endorse skip (real_compute=false), render, deliverables.

## 3. Budget allocation (flash run, ~6-8 rounds)
- R1: baseline (2 sims + 1 calc + 1 eval)
- R2: ceiling arch variant + funnel (additives) + eval
- R3: system candidate 1 (LNMO) full sim + eval
- R4: system candidate 2 (OKane2022 SiOx) full sim + eval
- R5: best + architecture + electrolyte + cooling combined
- R6: refinement / second variant
- R7+: fallback per diagnosis; three-strike questioning at 3 consecutive same-cause failures

## 4. Risk and fallback
- Risk 1: 500.94 Wh/kg near/above Li-metal level; library's best systems (LNMO/OKane2022) may cap ~400–500. If architecture space infeasible (3 strikes, same cause: ED gap) → question: system boundary (Li-metal approximation not available; electrode composition route), report negative honestly or switch direction.
- Risk 2: T_max at 4C 45 °C ambient — cooling h lever (10 → up to 1000 W/m²K) + thin electrodes; if T_max fails but ED passes → architecture/thermal scale fix (Stage 3), not material.
- Risk 3: plating at 4C — small negative particles + thin negative + high σ electrolyte; if plating fails → electrolyte transport scale (Stage 2 bridge) or negative thickness (Stage 3).
- Verify first: ED ceiling (determines whether materials mandatory), then safety gates.

## 5. References (direction → source)
- High-energy density requires material jump → "domain experience (no precise source)" + battery roadmap literature (USABC/DOE EV Everywhere targets ~350 Wh/kg cell; 500 Wh/kg requires Li metal or high-Si + high-V).
- LNMO high-voltage spinel 4.7 V → LNMO.json library parameter set (in-repo); LNMO review literature (Hu et al. / Manthiram high-voltage spinels) — mark "domain experience (no precise source)".
- SiOx anode capacity uplift → OKane2022 parameter set (O'Kane et al. 2022, lithium-ion battery degradation, J. Electrochem. Soc.) — in-repo parameter set.
- High-conductivity electrolyte for 4C plating mitigation → transport parameter literature (Valøen & Reimers 2005, conductivity of LiPF6 in carbonate mixtures) — domain memory, mark approximate.
- 4C fast charge without plating → plating onset potential modeling (OKane et al.; Yang et al. fast charge) — domain memory.

Honesty: no fabricated sources; where uncertain, marked.

